# THE DEFAULT REWARD FOR THIS LINEAGE (user 2026-10-14: "use v52 rewards and
# make that the default reward going forward").
#
# Source this from any launcher: `. slurm/v52_reward.env`. It is a single file
# rather than a block copied into each script because that copying is exactly
# how the arm ended up training against something else -- slurm/train_sac.sbatch
# inherited its exports from a smoke job and 21 terms silently fell back to CODE
# DEFAULTS, so off-road cost NOTHING, collisions did not terminate, and both
# lane penalties were half. A reward term that is not exported is not neutral.
#
# Values are read from the recorded run that works:
#   clean_fix1/results/run_env/carla_gated_v52_segvae_samesetup_t05.env
# v52: 1M steps, fault-ends eval SR 0.48 on trained Town05, 0.47 on held-out
# Town03. tests/test_reward_matches_v52.py fails if any term drifts from it.

# v52'S REWARD, TERM FOR TERM. This arm is meant to reuse the reward that
# actually trains in CARLA, and "meant to" is not the same as "does": the first
# version of this script inherited its exports from the smoke job, so 21 terms
# fell back to CODE DEFAULTS that are not v52's -- off-road cost NOTHING
# (EXPLORE_OFF_ROAD_PENALTY 10 -> 0), collisions were not terminal, and the lane
# penalties were half. Every value below is read from
# clean_fix1/results/run_env/carla_gated_v52_segvae_samesetup_t05.env and
# tests/test_reward_matches_v52.py fails if they drift again.
export EXPLORE_COLLISION_FATAL=1          # user 2026-10-14: collisions terminate
export EXPLORE_OFF_ROAD_PENALTY=10.0
export EXPLORE_LANE_PENALTY_NONE=5.0
export LANE_COLLISION_PENALTY=10.0
export LANE_DEPARTURE_PENALTY=10.0
export WEDGE_TRUNCATE=0
export GATED_GOAL_MAX_STEPS=1250
export EXPLORE_OFF_ROAD_FATAL=1 EXPLORE_LANE_MODE=terminal
export EXPLORE_EXEMPT_MARKS=NONE
export EXPLORE_GOAL_DIST_M=100
# PROGRESS ALONG THE LANE, not along the car's nose. v52 never exported this,
# so it ran on the code default `projected` (displacement . wp_forward). The
# arm's launcher set `heading` from its first commit (b23d1fb), and the test
# below could not see it: it only compared terms v52's env file names.
# `heading` pays a car driving tight circles on every step -- its displacement
# is always along its own nose -- and constant full lock also zeroes the
# steer-change penalty. v7's videos show exactly that: steer -0.93 to -1.00 in
# every sampled frame, both modes, 1000-step episodes. Found 2026-10-19.
export LANE_PROGRESS_MODE=projected
# INERT UNDER GATED_GOAL_REWARD=explore -- the goal arm is paid explore's reward,
# so these are read only by the sorb/progress kinds. Set to v52's values anyway,
# so the run's environment matches the recorded one exactly and the comparison
# has no "well, that one does not matter" exceptions to remember.
export GOAL_LANE_GRADED=1 GOAL_LANE_PENALTY=10.0 GOAL_LANE_PENALTY_BROKEN=10.0
export GOAL_LANE_PENALTY_NONE=5.0 GOAL_OFF_ROAD_PENALTY=10.0
export GOAL_OFFROAD_TRUNCATE_STEPS=1 GOAL_COLLISION_TRUNCATE_STEPS=1
export GOAL_TRUNCATE_COUNTS=1 ROUTE_POTENTIAL=1

# DEVIATION FROM v52, DELIBERATE (user 2026-10-14: "remove speed gating").
# v52 pays the progress term only below the target speed, so a car at or above
# it earns NOTHING for driving forward -- measured in run v3, where the per-step
# reward read -0.01 to -0.15 at throttle 0.7-0.88 while the car drove. With the
# gate off, forward progress always pays. The code default stays 1 so v52 itself
# remains reproducible; this file is where the run's choice is recorded.
export PROGRESS_SPEED_GATE=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLOSING THE CHEAP EXITS (my decision 2026-10-14, under the user's delegation
# "monitor and make decisions about reward"). The encoder and the observation
# are fixed by instruction; this is a reward change and nothing else.
#
# THE ARITHMETIC THAT FORCED IT, measured on the live v4 run: the realised
# return was -28.2 over 84 steps, about -0.34 a step. At gamma 0.99 that makes
#   continuing  ~ -0.34 / 0.01 = -34
#   crossing a line now          = -10, and the episode is over
# so ending the episode is worth +24 more than driving on. A critic that learns
# that is not broken, it is right -- and q_g sinking -0.49 -> -3.78 is it
# learning exactly that, as it did before both earlier collapses.
#
# With crossings and off-road FINED PER STEP instead of terminal, the geometry
# inverts: driving over a line costs -10 a step, far worse than the +0.5 a step
# that forward progress now pays (the speed gate is off), and there is no door
# to escape through. Driving properly becomes the best available policy rather
# than the hardest one.
#
# COLLISIONS STAY TERMINAL -- the user asked for that explicitly, and a wall is
# a door the agent has to seek out rather than one it drifts through.
#
# LANE CROSSINGS ARE TERMINAL AGAIN (user 2026-10-19: lane invasion and
# collision both terminal). This undoes the crossing half of the decision
# above, restoring v52's own rule (EXPLORE_LANE_MODE=terminal, set on the v52
# block at the top of this file; junction crossings and NONE marks stay
# forgiven). First run with it: v9, alongside v8 (crossings fined) to compare.
# Off-road is NOT terminal: the user named crossings and collisions only.
export EXPLORE_OFF_ROAD_FATAL=0

# BRAKE AT THE GOAL (user 2026-10-14: "the agent should brake near goal"), km/h.
# Above this, being inside the goal radius does NOT count as arriving: the bonus
# is withheld and the episode continues, so the car must slow down to collect
# it. 5 km/h is "slow", not "stopped dead" -- a stop-dead threshold would make
# arrival depend on a precision the policy has no way to practise yet.
#
# It has to be the arrival CONDITION rather than a penalty on speed: negative
# throttle is reverse and the progress term is ungated, so slowing already pays
# negatively and the reward otherwise wants maximum forward speed forever.
# (The value is set below, after v6 raised it from 5.)

# A DENSE GOAL TERM FOR GOAL MODE (my decision 2026-10-14, after v6).
# v6 ran the full 1M: the explore arm improved to 0.20 while the goal arm
# decayed 0.100 -> 0.010. Both modes are paid the SAME reward, so goal mode had
# nothing to make it behave differently -- only an arrival bonus it almost never
# collected. The policy optimised the objective that pays every step.
#
# POTENTIAL-BASED on route_remaining_m, so it cannot change which policy is
# optimal (Ng et al.) -- it only makes the existing optimum findable. K=1 puts
# it on the same scale as the progress term: both pay about 0.5 a step at
# driving speed, so closing on the goal is worth roughly twice merely driving.
export POTENTIAL_K=1

# ARRIVAL SPEED RAISED 5 -> 10 km/h. The ungated progress term pays for speed on
# every step while arrival pays once, so at 5 km/h the two fought and speed won;
# v6's goal episodes lengthened 840 -> 953 as the policy got faster. 10 km/h
# still requires braking from the 20 km/h target without demanding a crawl.
export GOAL_ARRIVAL_MAX_SPEED=10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AFTER v8 AND v9 (2026-10-19; user: "proceed with fixes - and restart").
#
# v9 made crossings TERMINAL (the user's 2026-10-19 rule) and never learned to
# stay in lane: episodes stuck at ~40 steps, goal arm 0.03-0.16 by 212k, against
# v8's 0.55 at the same point with crossings fined. The user approved going
# back to fines; this overrides the v52 `terminal` set at the top of the file.
export EXPLORE_LANE_MODE=penalise
#
# v8 then PARKED: peak goal arm 0.62 (~400k), and from episode 1920 the car sat
# motionless (92-100% still frames) with steer locked at +0.9. A parked step
# cost -0.03..-0.15, worth about -10 forever at gamma 0.99 -- one crossing's
# fine -- while v8's driving episodes often returned -1,000 to -3,500 on fines.
# Three changes, so parking stops being the safe answer:
#   * a crossing cost 3, not 10, so one mistake no longer outweighed parking
#     for the rest of the episode. REVERTED to v52's 10 on 2026-10-21 (user:
#     "make lane crossings -10"): v12's deterministic evals failed mostly on an
#     OPENING move -- steer ~-0.86, throttle ~0.3, creeping ~0.8 m over the
#     line on the left within 2-3 s (22 of 29 crossings within the first 3 m
#     at 1.8M). At 3 that creep was cheap in training; the idle charge below
#     now stops the 10 from making parking the cheaper answer, as it did in v8.
#     (No override here: the v52 block at the top sets 10.)
#   * standing still costs 0.5 a step below 2 km/h (parking forever ~ -50),
#     below the 10 km/h arrival speed so slowing to arrive stays free;
export EXPLORE_IDLE_PENALTY=0.5 EXPLORE_IDLE_SPEED_KMH=2
#   * explore arrival counts NET displacement from the start, not cumulative
#     path, which a car looping one junction also piles up (v8 episode 1360).
export EXPLORE_DIST_MODE=net

# LANE-CENTRE SHAPING (user 2026-10-25: image-goal navigation WITH lane
# following is the goal; chose "Both modes", then "Potential shaping"). v13
# crossed in 5/40 (best) to 23/40 (final) Town05 evals: in training a crossing
# never ended an episode, and nothing pointed at the centre, only the line.
# Potential c(s) from CARLA's map: 2.0 where the car's BODY meets the marking
# (quadratic: 0.5 halfway, ~0 centred; cap 4.5) + 1.0 at 45 deg heading error
# (cap there). Each step pays c(s) - 0.99 c(s'), c = 0 at a terminal state, so
# drifting to the line costs ~2 in total BEFORE the 10 fine and recovering pays
# it back, while the episode total is fixed by the start: no early crash can
# ever pay (the per-step cost first built had that risk). Sized freely because
# shaping cannot change the optimum; the crossing fine (10) is what prices
# crossings. Both modes; junctions forgiven; crossings fined, not terminal.
export LANE_CENTRE_K=2.0 LANE_HEADING_K=1.0
